# GIS-Source inspection safety (remember for further folders)

**Raw pack location:** `c:\AP-GIS\GIS-Source` (not under the app repo). Runtime layers remain the converted copies under `public/geo/gis-source/`.

When analyzing or integrating `GIS-Source` (Admin, OPS, Raster, etc.), **inspect actual content** (CRS, attributes, feature identity, era, size). Do **not** replace primary app layers by folder/filename alone.

## Recurring safety point types

1. **Geographic regime mismatch (era / admin split)**  
   Source may be older or undivided (e.g. pre-2014 AP+Telangana districts, IND_adm1 with no Telangana).  
   **Do not** replace primary drill, post-2014 AP state border, or India overview.  
   **May** expose as labeled historical/overlay-only layers.

2. **Same theme, different product**  
   e.g. border PS vs user PS KMZ; taluk vs NWIC mandals; SOI map-no **points** vs sheet **polygons** vs topo mosaic.  
   Keep complementary layers; fix legend/geometry to match real data; avoid duplicate “same id” layers.

3. **Payload / browser feasibility**  
   Huge vectors (e.g. full `ap_roads` ~153k) must not ship as one untiled GeoJSON.  
   Prefer independent subsets, tiling, or deferred dependent pipelines.

4. **CRS / projection**  
   PRJ text can disagree with coordinates (e.g. rail LCC metres). Always validate bbox; reproject before use.

5. **Explicit safety gate before replacement**  
   If GIS-Source conflicts with working primary data: run a content comparison (names, counts, Telangana/AP split, bbox).  
   Block replace when unsafe; document reason; integrate as overlay or subset instead.  
   Prefer GIS-Source only when content is the same kind of geography/product the feature needs.

